Author: anthnel <anthoni.devops@proton.me>
Date:   Mon Nov 23 17:28:06 2026 +0100

    fix(credentials): bound every host secret store call to 3 s (DEVDESK-745)

    DevDesk showed a blank screen at launch over SSH: the log stopped after
    the theme line. A goroutine dump of the hung process shows main blocked
    in credentials.Select -> KeyringAvailable -> go-keyring Get -> Secret
    Service Unlock -> handlePrompt, waiting with no timeout for the unlock
    prompt of the locked login collection, which nobody can answer over
    SSH. Select runs in app.New, before the first frame.

    Every HostStore call now goes through boundedHost, which runs it in a
    goroutine and gives up after keyringTimeout (3 s) with
    ErrKeyringUnresponsive. The probe and KeyringStorage Save, Load and
    Delete are covered. The call is abandoned, not cancelled (go-keyring
    has no context): while it stays blocked, later calls fail at once
    instead of waiting again and leaking another goroutine; once it
    returns, the store is asked again. A panic from the DEVDESK-610 guard
    is carried back to the caller so it still fails the test.

    Select treats a silent store like an absent one (auto: git helper then
    memory; pinned keyring: memory) and its Detail says the store did not
    answer, is probably locked, and how to get out of it.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: e12435fdf0a7

